  steps:
    1. Pick grid dimensions H in [13,19], W in [15,19]
    2. Pick num_rects in [1,4]; pick that many distinct non-bg colors
    3. For each rectangle pick width in [5,10] and height in [5,10]
    4. Place rectangles on the grid with no bounding-box overlap (gap >= 1 between any pair)
    5. Fill remaining cells with bg color 0
    6. Output is derived by applying the checkerboard rule to each rectangle interior
